The CG coefficients are extracted from the overlap alone: for each branch the overlaps at several grid points give linear equations on the unknown slice $\langle e_\nu\otimes e_1|\Psi_0\rangle$ (one equation per grid point, using the known $\varphi_u$), solved exactly for one-dimensional slices and by $2\times2$ systems for two-dimensional ones. The raw error is exactly $O(\epsilon)$ (ratio $4.00$ between $4\cdot10^{-6}$ and $10^{-6}$), and after Richardson extrapolation in $\epsilon$ the extracted slices equal the exact G-norm-1 HW-ket slices to $10^{-17}$--$10^{-21}$ (Table~\ref{tab:cgprec}); the exact values are listed in Appendix~\ref{app:CG}. For the adjoint the one-dimensional slices are $-1/\sqrt2,\ -1/\sqrt2,\ 0.1178511302$ for $(4,1,1),(3,3,0),(2,2,2)$ and the octet slices are $(0.04931160001,0.2088872897)$ and $(0.3379867346,-0.07978784486)$.

