## Multiplicity-2 sectors and universal mixing {#sec:mixing}

In a multiplicity-2 sector the HW space is two-dimensional and the untwisted copies of the HW ket are fixed by the eigenvectors of $S3c[1,2]=a_1$ restricted to it. We expected this to depend on $\theta$. It does not: $\theta_{12}\,S3c[1,2]|_{\rm HW}$ is a $\theta$-independent matrix with no scalar part (exact at $\theta=(2/7,-3/5),(1/5,-4/9),(3/7,-1/4)$), so the copies, and the mixing, are universal. For each sector we record the matrix $N_0=\theta_{12}\,S3c[1,2]|_{\rm HW}$ and the coordinate-ratio quadratic of its eigenvectors:

@table tab:univ | Universality of the multiplicity-2 mixing. $N_0=\theta_{12}S3c[1,2]|_{\rm HW}$ on the HW space (coordinates in the canonical rational HW basis of the data files), its trace and determinant, the eigenvalues $\alpha_\pm=(\mathrm{tr}\mp\sqrt{\mathrm{disc}})/2$ with $\mathrm{disc}=\mathrm{tr}^2-4\det$, and the quadratic satisfied by the ratio $r$ of the coordinates of the two eigenvectors. Sources: W2 task C, W3 cells 33, 35, 37; the adjoint matrix at $\theta_{12}=31/35$ is $(105/62)[[3,-1],[-1,7]]$.
@size small
@cols lcccc
| rep, sector | $N_0$ | tr, det | eigenvalues | $r$-quadratic |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| $[2,1,0]$ $(3,2,1)$ | $\tfrac32\begin{pmatrix}3&-1\\-1&7\end{pmatrix}$ | $15,\ 45$ | $(15\mp3\sqrt5)/2$ | $r^2+4r-1=0$ |
| $[3,1,0]$ $(5,2,1)$ | $\tfrac13\begin{pmatrix}19&-40\\-2&44\end{pmatrix}$ | $21,\ 84$ | $(21\mp\sqrt{105})/2$ | $40r^2+25r-2=0$ |
